---
description: Stackwise architecture, safety and current handoff status
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read README.md and AGENTS.md before changes. Communicate in Brazilian Portuguese.
- Preserve React 19, TanStack Start v1, file-based TanStack Router, Vite 7 and Tailwind CSS v4.
- Root and /login open /app/dashboard directly. Do not restore landing or login UI unless requested.
- Public UI access is not admin authorization. Validate private operations on the server using a real session and user_roles. Never use hardcoded credentials or client storage for authorization.
- Inventory currently uses a seeded in-memory store. Do not claim changes persist to Cloud without implementing and verifying persistence.
- Do not edit generated routeTree.gen.ts or generated integration clients. Add route files with matching createFileRoute IDs.
- Use createServerFn for internal server logic; authenticate private handlers. Verify callers of public webhook routes.
- Keep private credentials out of source and VITE_ variables. Never print .env or session tokens.
- Use semantic style tokens and existing UI components. Preserve Portuguese text.
- Historical PRDs and demo tests may be outdated; current code and explicit requirements take precedence.